  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1157 AM CDT Sat Oct 24 2026\n\nSkies were partly to mostly sunny early this afternoon with \ntemperatures in the middle 60s to lower 70s away from Lake \nMichigan. Temperatures should top out as warm as the middle 70s\nacross central Wisconsin. Meanwhile, a cold front across \nMinnesota will gradually push eastward into Wisconsin tonight, \nreaching north-central and central Wisconsin towards 12z Sunday. \nThe front will trigger a chance of showers late tonight into\nSunday morning. Looking to Sunday, several models are indicating\nan fgen band setting up across northern Wisconsin that could bring\na narrow area of showers. Only have 20-30% chance of rain for the\ntime being, but certainly could rain chances increased later \ntonight once there is better confidence in where the narrow\nline of showers develop. The chance of showers will linger into\nearly Sunday evening. Cooler temperatures will prevail as highs\nacross the north will be in the lower to middle 50s while it will\nstill be close to 70 degrees across east-central WI. Temperatures\nare going to be considerably cooler on Monday with highs in the\nmiddle 40s to middle 50s, which is more typical for late October.\n\nThe next chance of showers will be Monday night into Tuesday as \na warm front lifts northward. Highs on Tuesday will be in the\n50s to lower 60s. Above normal temperatures should then continue\ninto next weekend. The chances of rain return  late Tuesday night\nand Wednesday, and then again late Thursday night into next\nweekend as two systems move across the region.",
